<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $21.5 bln in Dec 2 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $21.5 bln in Dec 2 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $21.5 billion in the December 2 week to $3,814.1 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $20.6 billion to $4,862.8 billion. M-1 rose $14.6 billion to $1,089.1 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,799.0 billion versus $3,793.1 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
